  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Durable acceptance",
      "items": [
        "202 is written only after COMMIT of processing_jobs + outbox_messages (store.go 142-232)",
        "Survives API restart and RabbitMQ outage (Sprint 03 experiments 2, 3, 10)",
        "work_items.status is the client's business field; the async path never writes it"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Transport, not source of truth",
      "items": [
        "Numbers (1)-(3) are the synchronous request; letters (a)-(e) are asynchronous, after COMMIT (dashed)",
        "Publisher sets published_at only after a broker confirm; a crash between them causes a re-publish",
        "Worker ACKs only after the guarded DB write; redelivery is absorbed by state = 'accepted' guard"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Current recovery gap (evidence-backed, not fixed)",
      "items": [
        "Backup contract is pg_dump --data-only --table=public.work_items (tools/postgres-backup-local 156-165)",
        "processing_jobs and outbox_messages are outside the backup scope",
        "Destructive PostgreSQL loss + restore does not preserve accepted-but-unfinished async work",
        "A 202 is durable against process and broker failure, not against database loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Failure boundaries (Sprint 03 experiments)",
      "items": [
        "API restart after 202: rows are committed; a fresh publisher finds published_at NULL rows. No caller retry (exp 2, 10)",
        "RabbitMQ down: acceptance and /ready need only PostgreSQL; outbox rows wait until the broker returns (exp 3)",
        "Worker crash before (e): redelivery; guarded UPDATE sees a terminal state and ACKs without a second effect (exp 4, 5)",
        "PostgreSQL down: API not ready; worker NACK-requeues without inventing an attempt (exp 11)",
        "Destructive DB loss + restore: only work_items returns. Not an experiment result; follows from backup scope"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown / not claimed",
      "items": [
        "Worker processing step is a no-op (processor.go 24)",
        "Reject(false) with no dead-letter exchange discards malformed messages",
        "Outbox claim lock is not held during publish; several API replicas could double-publish",
        "Queued messages surviving a broker restart is configured, not experimentally shown",
        "No exactly-once delivery or publication"
      ]
    }
  ]
